{
  "_comment": "Free-endpoint model routing. Every entry is a free prototyping endpoint on the same key; nothing here is a paid endpoint. The router tries 'chain' in order and auto-falls-back when a model errors, times out or hits a rate limit.",
  "_chain_note": "The lead model of each tier must answer on the free endpoint. Verified 30 Oct 2026: deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4.1-flash hangs past 30s even on a four-token prompt and z-ai/glm-5.3 answers 410 Gone. Verified again on 01 Nov 2026 during a live run: minimaxai/minimax-m3.1-flash answered 429 rate limited and both nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b and stepfun-ai/step-5-preview then hung past their timeouts, so a chat request failed after 105 seconds. Every tier now leads with nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b or nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b, which answered a 2373-token reply in 5.25 seconds. The three picked models stay in the chains and in the aliases; the router also retires a model that times out or is gone, so a dead lead can never block a request again.",
